{"chunk_id": "9fa6d0913fa5", "text": "King Dasaratha asks the sage Rishyasringa how he might obtain an heir. The sage promises that the king will father four sons and begins the Putrakameshti sacrifice described in the Atharva Veda. As the ritual proceeds, celestial beings gather, but they soon appeal to Brahma with a grave complaint: the rakshasa king Ravana, empowered by boons, tyrannizes the three worlds and even humiliates the gods. Brahma reveals the flaw in Ravana\u2019s protection\u2014he asked immunity from gods and spirits but dismissed humans as insignificant. At that moment Vishnu appears, and the gods implore him to be born as Dasaratha\u2019s son and destroy Ravana. Vishnu agrees, vowing to incarnate as four sons of the king and end the demon\u2019s reign, setting in motion the divine origin of Rama and his brothers.\nThe gods complain to Brahma about Ravana, leading Vishnu to resolve to incarnate as Dasaratha\u2019s four sons to destroy the tyrant.\nThemes: divine incarnation, cosmic justice, Ravana's tyranny, boons and loopholes, divine intervention", "vector": [0.007555935997515917, -0.017831744626164436, -0.02102925255894661, -0.014315811917185783, 0.001789476489648223, 0.020856771618127823, -0.02775595895946026, -0.01600080542266369, -0.038476232439279556, -0.005751533433794975, 0.003449593437835574, 0.008663786575198174, 0.006710122339427471, 0.016743795946240425, -0.009061816148459911, 0.017261235043406487, 0.04213811084628105, -0.03584923595190048, 0.0396437868475914, 0.007960599847137928, 0.0028624990954995155, -0.03157704696059227, 0.0037846018094569445, 0.018402254208922386, -0.024054279550909996, 0.006899186875671148, 0.020803701132535934, -0.01886662282049656, 0.021440548822283745, -0.004030053969472647, -0.0013491559075191617, -0.020485278218984604, 0.004643683321774006, -0.01197406928986311, -0.022966330870985985, 0.00972520001232624, 0.002315207850188017, -0.01254457887262106, 0.012405267916619778, -0.011270882561802864, 0.00082218070747